# Rank 1260 / CVE-2022-43416 (SECURITY-2844): the Katalon Studio Engine
# Plugin's ExecuteKatalonStudioHelper sent an anonymous hudson.remoting.Callable
# across the Jenkins channel to run Katalon Studio, with a checkRoles override
# left empty -- nothing ever calls RoleChecker.check, so the callable does not
# restrict which channel role may enter call(). The fix drops the raw
# Callable/RoleChecker pair and extends jenkins.security.MasterToSlaveCallable,
# whose own checkRoles already enforces the expected role.
#
# ATTENTION, engine gap. internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/java.go's expr()
# handling of "object_creation_expression" (java.go:1234-1244) converts `new T(args)
# { ... }` to a bare nir.Call{Callee: Name{ID: typ}, Path: typ, Method: typ} and never
# reads the node's "body" field, so a Java anonymous class body -- the class_body
# holding the overridden call()/checkRoles() methods here -- is dropped entirely
# during parsing. No ClassDef, no FuncDef, no class-context event exists for it: the
# checkRoles/call methods, and the fact this anonymous class implements Callable, are
# invisible to every binding. Confirmed with a minimal pair: the same checkRoles/call
# shape written as a *named* top-level class (`public class X implements Callable`)
# is caught by the new JenkinsRemotingCallableMissingRoleCheck binding below (verified
# directly with `vyql explain` against a standalone repro); the identical shape as an
# anonymous inner class -- which is what the real vulnerable and patched code both use
# -- produces no findings either way, vulnerable or patched, because the class_body is
# never parsed to begin with. `vyql resolve` on the real code shows only
# analysis.class.context for the *enclosing* named class
# (ExecuteKatalonStudioHelper) at line 13; no analysis.class.context or
# analysis.function.context event exists anywhere for the anonymous Callable's own
# body (the object_creation_expression spanning the launcher.getChannel().call(...)
# argument).
#
# Not mechanical: anonymous class bodies are common far beyond Jenkins Callables
# (Runnable, Comparator, ActionListener, TimerTask, anonymous interface
# implementations generally), and giving them nir representation needs a new
# statement/expression shape -- object_creation_expression appears as a nested
# expression (here, an argument to .call()), not a standalone statement, so there is
# no existing statement slot to hang a ClassDef off of; the fix has to decide how an
# expression-position construct emits an additional top-level nir node and how that
# node's methods get scoped, resolved, and connected into the call graph
# (`launcher.getChannel().call(anonymousCallable)` needs to resolve into the
# anonymous class's call() body for taint to reach KatalonUtils.executeKatalon at
# all). That is new classification and a new call-resolution relation, not a missing
# switch case, and it would touch every language frontend and binding that scopes on
# "class" or "function", so it stays out of this loop. Blocks any Java CVE whose
# vulnerable or patched shape lives inside an anonymous class body -- this rank, and
# any future rank shaped the same way.
#
# The JenkinsRemotingCallableMissingRoleCheck binding added alongside this spec is
# independently useful: it generalizes the already-shipped
# JenkinsRemotingCallableSystemPropertiesLeak binding (VYQL-SEC-013, scoped to
# callables that leak System.getProperties) to the class of Jenkins remoting
# Callables whose checkRoles never calls RoleChecker.check, regardless of what
# call() does -- the same fix (extend MasterToSlaveCallable) resolves both, and
# Jenkins' own remoting documentation describes checkRoles this way independent of
# any one CVE. It fires on this rank's exact vulnerability when written as the more
# common named-class shape (verified directly, not through this spec, since the
# spec's job is to model the real code); it cannot fire on the anonymous-class shape
# the real fix commit actually uses, for the reason above.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap

test "rank1260: raw Callable with an empty checkRoles runs Katalon on any role"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/com/katalon/jenkins/plugin/helper/ExecuteKatalonStudioHelper.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-113
  reject_review code.JenkinsRemotingCallableMissingRoleCheck
  code
  ```
  package com.katalon.jenkins.plugin.helper;

  import hudson.EnvVars;
  import hudson.FilePath;
  import hudson.Launcher;
  import hudson.model.TaskListener;
  import hudson.remoting.Callable;
  import org.jenkinsci.remoting.RoleChecker;

  import java.util.HashMap;
  import java.util.Map;

  public class ExecuteKatalonStudioHelper {

      public static boolean executeKatalon(
              FilePath workspace,
              EnvVars buildEnvironment,
              Launcher launcher,
              TaskListener taskListener,
              String version,
              String location,
              String executeArgs,
              String x11Display,
              String xvfbConfiguration) {
          try {
              return launcher.getChannel().call(new Callable<Boolean, Exception>() {
                  @Override
                  public Boolean call() throws Exception {
                      if (workspace != null) {
                          String workspaceLocation = workspace.getRemote();
                          if (workspaceLocation != null) {
                              Map<String, String> environmentVariables = new HashMap<>();
                              environmentVariables.putAll(System.getenv());
                              return KatalonUtils.executeKatalon(
                                  version,
                                  location,
                                  workspaceLocation,
                                  executeArgs,
                                  x11Display,
                                  xvfbConfiguration,
                                  environmentVariables);
                          }
                      }
                      return true;
                  }
                  @Override
                  public void checkRoles(RoleChecker roleChecker) throws SecurityException {
                  }
              });
          } catch (Exception e) {
              return false;
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1260: MasterToSlaveCallable enforces the expected role for the same run"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/com/katalon/jenkins/plugin/helper/ExecuteKatalonStudioHelper.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-113
  reject_review code.JenkinsRemotingCallableMissingRoleCheck
  code
  ```
  package com.katalon.jenkins.plugin.helper;

  import hudson.EnvVars;
  import hudson.FilePath;
  import hudson.Launcher;
  import hudson.model.TaskListener;
  import jenkins.security.MasterToSlaveCallable;

  import java.util.HashMap;
  import java.util.Map;

  public class ExecuteKatalonStudioHelper {

      public static boolean executeKatalon(
              FilePath workspace,
              EnvVars buildEnvironment,
              Launcher launcher,
              TaskListener taskListener,
              String version,
              String location,
              String executeArgs,
              String x11Display,
              String xvfbConfiguration) {
          try {
              return launcher.getChannel().call(new MasterToSlaveCallable<Boolean, Exception>() {
                  @Override
                  public Boolean call() throws Exception {
                      if (workspace != null) {
                          String workspaceLocation = workspace.getRemote();
                          if (workspaceLocation != null) {
                              Map<String, String> environmentVariables = new HashMap<>();
                              environmentVariables.putAll(System.getenv());
                              return KatalonUtils.executeKatalon(
                                  version,
                                  location,
                                  workspaceLocation,
                                  executeArgs,
                                  x11Display,
                                  xvfbConfiguration,
                                  environmentVariables);
                          }
                      }
                      return true;
                  }
              });
          } catch (Exception e) {
              return false;
          }
      }
  }
  ```
